{
  "_comment": "SPINE-1. Faithful port of thaumcraft.common.blocks.BlockCustomOre.getDrops (1.7.10): meta 0 (cinnabar) drops the ore itself (furnace-smelted to quicksilver later); metas 1-6 (infused stone) drop itemshard meta md-1, q = 1 + rand.nextInt(2 + fortune) single stacks (the original loop adds q stacks of 1, so rolls carry the count and each stack is size 1); meta 7 (amber bearing stone) drops itemresource meta 6, 1 + rand.nextInt(fortune + 1) via uniform_bonus_count(bonusMultiplier=1) == 1 + rand(1+fortune). Silk touch: the original getDrops has NO silk branch because 1.7.10 vanilla Block.harvestBlock short-circuits to the block item (canSilkHarvest true, damageDropped(meta)=meta) before getDrops runs, so the silk pool drops the block itself with the variant preserved. Exp (rand(0,3) for 1-6, rand(1,4) for 7) is not expressible in a loot table and lives in BlockCustomOre.getExpDrop.",
